  "query_preview": "..\nSynopsis:\nA couple cut-off lows exist over the region. The one just to our\nnorth is expected to drift east into Manitoba today. The other low\nis dropping SW from British Columbia and is expected to remain \noff the Pac NW coast for the next few days.\n\nSkies have cleared early this morning with high humidity that has\nallowed some fog to form briefly. The big question this morning is\nwill the fog become widespread and dense before the sun burns it\noff by afternoon. The NBM favors it to form over the lower Milk\nand Missouri River valleys but HREF is showing less confidence for\nfog. With the low confidence, will hold off on any headlines for\nthis.\n\nWith the upper low over BC, the zonal flow today and Thursday \nwill become more meridional as a ridge over the Eastern Montana is\ninduced. This won't boost temps much but will send moisture in on\nFriday in the form of clouds.\n\nPrecip chances do increase over the weekend with the highest\nchances for rain coming Sunday night.\n\nClearing is expected behind the system early next week with an\nupper ridge bringing in drier conditions.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThere were no deviations from the NBM, but confidence on its\nhandling of the fog is low. The HREF is showing low confidence on\nthe fog so widespread dense fog is not expected at this time. TFJ",
